      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the smallest number of gold coins (let's call it \\( N \\)) that meets the following conditions:\n1. When divided among six people, four coins are left over.\n2. When divided among five people, three coins are left over.\n3. We need to find the remainder when these coins are divided among seven people.\n\nLet's represent these conditions using modular arithmetic:\n1. \\( N \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6} \\)\n2. \\( N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\)\n3. We need to find \\( N \\mod 7 \\).\n\nFirst, let's solve the equations \\( N \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6} \\) and \\( N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\):\n\nFrom \\( N \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6} \\), we can write \\( N = 6k + 4 \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\nSubstitute this into \\( N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\):\n\\[ 6k + 4 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\\[ 6k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{5} \\]\n\\[ k \\equiv -1 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSince \\(-1 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5}\\), we have:\n\\[ k \\equiv 4 \\pmod{5} \\]\nSo,\n\\[ k = 5m + 4 \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( k = 5m + 4 \\) back into \\( N = 6k + 4 \\):\n\\[ N = 6(5m + 4) + 4 = 30m + 24 + 4 = 30m + 28 \\]\nThus, \\( N \\equiv 28 \\pmod{30} \\).\n\nNow we need to find \\( N \\mod 7 \\). Using \\( N = 30m + 28 \\):\n\\[ N \\equiv 28 \\pmod{28} \\]\nSo, we need \\( N \\mod 7 \\):\n\\[ N \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\nThus, the number of coins left when divided among seven people is \\( \\boxed{0} \\).\n\nTo ensure accuracy, let's verify with Python code.\n```python\n# Finding the smallest number N that satisfies the given conditions\n# N ≡ 4 (mod 6)\n# N ≡ 3 (mod 5)\n\n# We can start by listing numbers that satisfy N ≡ 4 (mod 6)\n# Then check if they satisfy N ≡ 3 (mod 5)\n\ndef find_remainder_when_divided_by_7():\n    # Find N that satisfies 0 <= N < 210 (since we are looking at small numbers, we might initialize very large enough)\n    return next(n for n in range(210) if (n % 30 == 28) and (n % 7 == 0))  # We need to check for the smallest n\n\n# Determine the remainder when divided by 7\nremainder = find_remainder_when_divided_by_7()\nprint(remainder)\n```",
